{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward","id":972504,"title":"Penetrating a Correspondance Ward ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T07:20:24-07:00","id":972504,"title":"Penetrating a Correspondance Ward ?","content":"A mage has set up a ward on a small farm house that prevents all entry except for those who have been ''whitelisted.'', M20 states that Werecreatures are able to penetrate said Correspondence ward by rolling wits + occult at a difficulty of 6 or the mage's arete, whatever is higher and the dice is limited to their Rage/Gnosis, whatever is higher. i come from a community where mages pump their wards with 40+ successes, and as a werecreature, how am i supposed to beat 40+ successes with only 7 dice to roll against it ? thus making the task impossible to achieve by anyone other than a Mage, if that is so, then why is their explanations on how Werecreatures/Vampires could penetrate said ward while it's impossibe? are the book authors under the impression that a Mage will not exceed 5+ successes on a ward ? or is it practically impossible to penetrate a Correspondence ward that has been stacked with heavy successes like 30+ ? Werecreatures are not able to perform extended rolls to countermagick it either, and is it possible for 5-7 wolves to gather up and combine their successes to achieve a enough successes to penetrate a ward together? or is that just not possible ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:22:32-07:00","id":972507,"title":"","content":"Get more than one Garou to roll. Alternately, don't use Mage mages in crossovers, because they weren't made to be in anything other than in an Ars Magica-revival universal reality warper setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:27:10-07:00","id":972511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972507#post972507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get more than one Garou to roll. Alternately, don't use Mage mages in crossovers, because they weren't made to be in anything other than in an Ars Magica-revival universal reality warper setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh trust me..Mages wouldnt be a thing if i was the storyteller in the current chronicle i partake in, and thank you for the quick reply aswell, seems reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:45:17-07:00","id":972521,"title":"","content":"Mages should not have been able to accumulate 40+ successes, as each additional roll to accumulate successes is an additional +1 difficulty (at least in Revised). Even so, just bypass it through the Umbra. It is a spatial filter, not an interdimentional filter. Alternatively, find a few Sorcerers to tear it down with Unweaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:18:26-07:00","id":972533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972521#post972521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages should not have been able to accumulate 40+ successes, as each additional roll to accumulate successes is an additional +1 difficulty (at least in Revised). Even so, just bypass it through the Umbra. It is a spatial filter, not an interdimentional filter. Alternatively, find a few Sorcerers to tear it down with Unweaving.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're talking about stacking successes without a ritual.<br /> <br /> If I recall right, there are Gifts to tear through wards. Books also say that wards are quite effective ways of defense due to their mechanics (and as such there are quotes to that), and there are rules for crossover in there too.<br /> <br /> As for your question, you can sidestep and by-pass the said ward, unless Spirit 4 was used on top of that as well and the threshold was set in the Umbra too.<br /> <br /> In that case, you can try teleporting inside. If it was protected against teleportation too with additional successes, then --<br /> <br /> Seek what can disrupt threshold. If it's set on the ground in a form of &quot;line&quot; or &quot;circle&quot;, think about it - maybe you can do something about the ground where ward stands? If it's set on the item, try to affect the said item so it's out of the way. If you, for whatever reason cannot access threshold (though I have hard time imagining why wouldn't you be able to), then --<br /> <br /> Try seeking whoever can access the warded area. If you cannot (or you ran out of options), then --<br /> <br /> Get another mage to disrupt the ward + do your own countermagick on top. If that's not an option as well, then --<br /> <br /> You could try getting there from above. Setting up the ward needs to have a threshold, and the air isn't a stable enough threshold, thus it's quite challenging to make it &quot;above&quot;.<br /> <br /> And if I guessed it right who you are, I doubt that whoever you're facing against is as knowledged and versed in mage ways to get certain ideas and manage to set the ward on the air and make it legitimate as well (well if you actually are who I think you are, don't mind my past mistake with rituals, you're getting a response after all and quite few ways).<br /> <br /> Good luck in whatever you're doing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:24:31-07:00","id":972538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972521#post972521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages should not have been able to accumulate 40+ successes, as each additional roll to accumulate successes is an additional +1 difficulty (at least in Revised). Even so, just bypass it through the Umbra. It is a spatial filter, not an interdimentional filter. Alternatively, find a few Sorcerers to tear it down with Unweaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the ward has Spirit Sphere involved, does it block accesses from the Umbra ? pretty sure it does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:33:24-07:00","id":972543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>onedayumay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward#post972504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage has set up a ward on a small farm house that prevents all entry except for those who have been ''whitelisted.'', M20 states that Werecreatures are able to penetrate said Correspondence ward by rolling wits + occult at a difficulty of 6 or the mage's arete, whatever is higher and the dice is limited to their Rage/Gnosis, whatever is higher. i come from a community where mages pump their wards with 40+ successes, and as a werecreature, how am i supposed to beat 40+ successes with only 7 dice to roll against it ? thus making the task impossible to achieve by anyone other than a Mage, if that is so, then why is their explanations on how Werecreatures/Vampires could penetrate said ward while it's impossibe? are the book authors under the impression that a Mage will not exceed 5+ successes on a ward ? or is it practically impossible to penetrate a Correspondence ward that has been stacked with heavy successes like 30+ ? Werecreatures are not able to perform extended rolls to countermagick it either, and is it possible for 5-7 wolves to gather up and combine their successes to achieve a enough successes to penetrate a ward together? or is that just not possible ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can roll your inherent countermagick multiple times,each success reduce the success used for the ward.<br /> Roll until you get a Total ammount of 40 success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:36:34-07:00","id":972544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972543#post972543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can roll your inherent countermagick multiple times,each success reduce the success used for the ward.<br /> Roll until you get a Total ammount of 40 success.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not how it works, else wards wouldn't be so effective at all. (Though there is optional rules about that, and at some points wards don't even work on supernaturals)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if the ward has Spirit Sphere involved, does it block accesses from the Umbra ? pretty sure it does. </div> </div> </div>They need to set the threshold in Penumbra as well and spend successes for that. It's a lengthy process to do so.<br /> <br /> If they haven't done that, it doesn't apply in Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:50:37-07:00","id":972614,"title":"","content":"I won't touch on the 40+ success angle.. I would just say if they can't go in via the umbra, then just pop out just OUTSIDE the place and enter normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:33:09-07:00","id":972647,"title":"","content":"A creative attempt would be to \u201chack\u201c the whitelist.<br /> Depends a little on the style of the ward but it should be possible to find a spirit that adds you to the whitelist.<br /> A whitelist is an inherent weakness after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:40:49-07:00","id":972841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972533#post972533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If I recall right, there are Gifts to tear through wards. Books also say that wards are quite effective ways of defense due to their mechanics (and as such there are quotes to that), and there are rules for crossover in there too.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Gifts to tear through wards that I can think of are Rank 6 Garou Gifts and a Rank 4 Rokea Gift. Otherwise, running Correspondance Bans like that make them work completely (and uncontested) against every single Supernatural in the WoD that isn't a Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972533#post972533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, you can try teleporting inside. If it was protected against teleportation too with additional successes, then --</div> </div> </div> </div>Teleporting isn't something Garou generally have access to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972533#post972533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Seek what can disrupt threshold. If it's set on the ground in a form of &quot;line&quot; or &quot;circle&quot;, think about it - maybe you can do something about the ground where ward stands? If it's set on the item, try to affect the said item so it's out of the way. If you, for whatever reason cannot access threshold (though I have hard time imagining why wouldn't you be able to), then --</div> </div> </div> </div> Now this is a fair enough point. You should be able to damage/destroy whatever the material setup for the Ward is. If the Ward has sigils or runes carved along the inside of the building, you should be able to physically knock down a wall or otherwise mar/destroy said sigils to disrupt the Ban (you would have to use toolls of some sort, since in theory Outsiders couldn't touch the walls otherwise). But that again is completely up to ST interpretation. Quite a bit of Mage ends up that way, and so any advice from the forums are merely suggestion on what <i>may</i> work as opposed to solutions that will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972533#post972533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get another mage to disrupt the ward + do your own countermagick on top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because only Mages can defeat Mages according to Mage. (this isn't even sarcastic. this has generally been my experience)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972533#post972533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could try getting there from above. Setting up the ward needs to have a threshold, and the air isn't a stable enough threshold, thus it's quite challenging to make it &quot;above&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not that it matters, but I don't agree that that's how Bans work. You shouldn't just be able to jump (or fly or whatever) over them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972544#post972544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how it works, else wards wouldn't be so effective at all. (Though there is optional rules about that, and at some points wards don't even work on supernaturals)</div> </div> </div> </div>Having asked about a relatively similar situation just recently on the Mage forums, there doesn't actually seem to be an exact way that it works. Like tons of other things in Mage, how Bans works is left completely up to the ST running the game. This would be a perfectly acceptable tactic in some games and ruled completely differently in others. I personally (after the previously mentioned thread) like the idea that a Ban can be beaten down eventually. Otherwise you set up a world where only Mages can go up against Mages. There is no way for <i>any other Supernatural</i> to counter anything Mages do. Bans and Wards are completely unbeatable, even to Incarna level Spirits because of how the system is set up. There is something fundamentally wrong with that point of view to me.<br /> <br /> So I came to the conclusion that (for my games) I think non-Mage Supernaturals should be able to work to take down Mage protections eventually. Mind you, the Mages inside can and should be bolstering their Wards at the same time, leading to a drawn out siege. I view that as a much more acceptable setup then just saying Mages win and there's nothing anyone can ever do about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-19-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:51:38-07:00","id":972846,"title":"","content":"I just let supernaturals buy Counterspells (from Hedge Magic rather than Sorcerer (Revised)), even if I do not normally allow them to buy Numina. It tends to level the playing field quite effectively, though you have to figure out how Unweaving works in that case. At three bonus points (or experience points) each, they are also not that expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:24:54-07:00","id":972860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972841#post972841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleporting isn't something Garou generally have access to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there moon bridges and various Gifts that use them, and that one Bone Gnawer power that lets them dive into one dumpster and emerge in a different one. They;re all higher rank, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:55:49-07:00","id":972871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972860#post972860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there moon bridges and various Gifts that use them, and that one Bone Gnawer power that lets them dive into one dumpster and emerge in a different one. They;re all higher rank, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I thought of moon bridges but assume that if the Umbra is blocked via Spirit, they should be as well. They're not teleporting in the Mage sense I wouldn't think.<br /> The dumpster one is new in guessing? In any case I didn't know about it. Thanks. Works similar to Backbite?<br /> <br /> I have all of the W20 books out so far (and have read out skimmed them), but since I haven't gotten to play/run it yet, I'm less familiar with the new stuff than Revised. And even that I haven't really gotten to play in a decade\ud83d\ude41","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T22:14:24-07:00","id":972944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Bogdan</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972533#post972533\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">You could try getting there from above. Setting up the ward needs to have a threshold, and the air isn't a stable enough threshold, thus it's quite challenging to make it &quot;above&quot;.</span><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br /> Not that it matters, but I don't agree that that's how Bans work. You shouldn't just be able to jump (or fly or whatever) over them. </div> </div> </div>Dunno', I figured it would be actually quite legitimate. Of course, you can't just &quot;jump&quot; over warded line (though, if you can jump really high, maybe you can) because wards require threshold, always.<br /> <br /> And that's where the trick comes in. How far can you stretch your ward and what kind of a threshold you can access to? Wards are indeed very strong and the system favors Mages excessively, but if you cannot let other supernaturals counter them through system (or you can, but ruling out that anyone can just keep stacking countermagick successes makes wards very ineffective, and it basically means that other supernaturals tear down wards easier than other Mages who are actually the magick guys), why not let them counter the wards the other way if they have enough wit?<br /> <br /> A mage has travelling ward on him? Seek whatever the mage possesses, be it clothes or some iron item, or whatever. The rule of &quot;Pressing the Ward&quot; will apply, and you should attack the Mage with what he has in order to by-pass his protection.<br /> <br /> A mage has set protection over some area? Seek your way around threshold, burrow and go underneath, go through Umbra, or even go from above (though one problem with it is the fact that if Mage turns out smart enough, he could set the threshold even above. Note, air isn't solid enough to be threshold, so it can get quite challenging to pull off and ensure it's legit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:03:56-07:00","id":972950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972944#post972944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why not let them counter the wards the other way if they have enough wit?</div> </div> </div> </div> the Mages should also be assumed to have wit. Far more than others, considering that we're talking in reference to how their own powers work. This setup let's Mages put some time in and have unbeatable magic come out. You are literally letting them stack (in this case 40) successes and having the other Supernaturals roll a single Attribute+ Ability dicepool (usually only up to 10 dice) to counter, which is impossible for anything (even Methuselahs and powerful spirits) to overcome. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage has travelling ward on him? Seek whatever the mage possesses, be it clothes or some iron item, or whatever. The rule of &amp;quot;Pressing the Ward&amp;quot; will apply, and you should attack the Mage with what he has in order to by-pass his protection.<br /> <br /> A mage has set protection over some area? Seek your way around threshold, burrow and go underneath, go through Umbra, or even go from above (though one problem with it is the fact that if Mage turns out smart enough, he could set the threshold even above. Note, air isn't solid enough to be threshold, so it can get quite challenging to pull off and ensure it's legit) </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't usually allow burrowing under a ward either. It goes against the spirit of a Ward. As per there being a upper threshold to the Ward, I would think that would have a lot more to do with paradigm than anything else. I suppose that applies to the burrowing thing as well now that I think about it. But if a house is inscribed with Runes to prevent entry, above or below those Runes would work (imo). If incense were the focus, my interpretation would be more fluid, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:11:16-07:00","id":972954,"title":"","content":"There are not a lot of reasonable ways to overcome 40+ success wards. If unreasonable things are then up for suggestion, perhaps you could try to summon a Nameless or a Nexus Crawler and see if they could break reality enough to turn everything into cottage cheese.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:22:53-07:00","id":972960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=972950#post972950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the Mages should also be assumed to have wit. Far more than others, considering that we're talking in reference to how their own powers work. This setup let's Mages put some time in and have unbeatable magic come out. You are literally letting them stack (in this case 40) successes and having the other Supernaturals roll a single Attribute+ Ability dicepool (usually only up to 10 dice) to counter, which is impossible for anything (even Methuselahs and powerful spirits) to overcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't usually allow burrowing under a ward either. It goes against the spirit of a Ward. As per there being a upper threshold to the Ward, I would think that would have a lot more to do with paradigm than anything else. I suppose that applies to the burrowing thing as well now that I think about it. But if a house is inscribed with Runes to prevent entry, above or below those Runes would work (imo). If incense were the focus, my interpretation would be more fluid, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But if you do allow any supernatural to roll Attribute + Abillity endlessly, not only it makes weird mechanics that supernaturals are more effective in dealing with wards (countermagicking them) than Mages themselves, but it also makes wards ineffective.<br /> <br /> It's quite a tough decision. You either make their wards ineffective and enforce weird mechanics, or lessen the effectiveness by Ban itself in the way I described. To each their own, but imho the second would be better.<br /> <br /> And dunno', but in my Mage experience, I had to think about what I'm doing whenever Storyteller would come up with something and had to use my wit instead of just throwing stats around. I also took notice that Mages have to prepare beforehand for many things such as setting up various defenses, enhances and more, else they just cannot quite keep up with supernaturals in quick combat.<br /> <br /> Also, about burrowing, I'm more than assured it could work because - well hey, once you set the ward, it cannot just go beneath to limitless distances, right? That'd create really weird physics, and influence even of a single ward would be rather vast.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:41:40-07:00","id":973184,"title":"","content":"Going above, under etc, I think that's cancelled because if the mage had increased the range (making its protective effects expand more than the threshold/surface of said ward, (through expenditure of extra Quintessence), it should be in all directions. While it wouldn't go limitlessly to all directions, it might as well go down and up and to the sides 3m, 6m, 9m, depending on how much Quintessence and successes the mage dedicated to range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","user":"Rotwood","date":". 09-20-2016, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:59:46-07:00","id":973194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>onedayumay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward#post972504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A mage has set up a ward on a small farm house that prevents all entry except for those who have been ''whitelisted.''</div> </div> </div> </div>Going way back to the OP, what Spheres are involved in setting up the Ward? Because I realized that the Ward is set up to keep everything but a few out. It is much much easier to set up a Ward vs something, as opposed to a Ward vs Everything except something.<br /> <br /> And just to hazard a guess, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12132_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12132\" data-vbnamecard=\"12132\">Bogdan</a> is the (or one of the) STs? If so, then any advice from the forums that contradicts their point of view is kind of useless anyways. So much of Mage is left completely up to ST interpretation that getting outside points of view becomes problematic at best. And with Bans specifically, there seems to be completely different opinions on how they work, both in how the prevent entry (direction-wise) and how solid they are. So when in doubt, talk to your ST. If they say Sphere Magick can only be overcome/countered by Mages, then that is that. You could throw a hundred Nexus Crawlers at the house and the Wards could protect it.<br /> <br /> Oh, and mind you, none of this discussion has taken Paradigms into account, which is arguably just as or more important than the Spheres or mechanics involved in Wards/Bans(so really, 3 separate components). But in my experience (unfortunately), Paradigms are used as an afterthought in general. <i>How</i> the Wards are set up should be just as important as the mechanics involved and Spheres used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-20-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:13:31-07:00","id":973466,"title":"","content":"How can a Mage get 40+ successes on any roll though? Each successive roll is a +1 difficulty, and you can only spend a maximum of three Quintessence per turn. Even if you had unlimited Quintessence, the difficulty should exceed the maximum potential roll long before you get to 40+ successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:19:44-07:00","id":973471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=973466#post973466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can a Mage get 40+ successes on any roll though? Each successive roll is a +1 difficulty, and you can only spend a maximum of three Quintessence per turn. Even if you had unlimited Quintessence, the difficulty should exceed the maximum potential roll long before you get to 40+ successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is for extended rolls. Ritual rolls have a different system that doesn't get the +1 dif per roll modifier.<br /> <br /> That's why Mage players always cast anything they can ritually before leaving the house At least that's how it was in Revised (from memory).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-20-2016, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:56:07-07:00","id":973497,"title":"","content":"Ritual rolls do not harbor a +1 difficulty modifiers per roll unless you've exhausted your Stamina and needed to take a break, at that point there're specific mechanics on how to continue with the ritual at a later date (there's a different system regarding increased difficulty). You can channel more than three Quintessence points per turn - it's restricted to your Avatar's rating, <i>until</i> the character has Prime 3 that is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amount of Quintessence Used</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game-wise, a mage must have at least three dots in either the Prime or Primal Utility Spheres if she wants to use \u201cmore than her share\u201d of energy. Any mage with an Avatar Background can absorb that Background\u2019s worth of Quintessence from a Node or Tass, or use the points of Quintessence in the Quintessence wheel on her character sheet. In order to use more points of Quintessence than she has in her Avatar Background rating, however, and in order to use Quintessence from other sources, she must have at least Rank 3 in the Prime or Primal Utility Spheres. As an example, Jinx (Avatar 5) can use up to five points of Quintessence per turn, while Sabra, (Avatar 1) may use only one point of Quintessence per turn until he achieves Prime 3.<br /> <br /> As the Base Damage and Duration chart explains, the amount of Quintessence a mage with Prime 3 or higher mage can employ within a single Effect is based upon the number of successes rolled. If Penny Dreadful\u2019s player, for example, rolls three successes, then Penny can employ up to six points of Quintessence with that Effect; if she rolls five, then Penny can use up to 10 points that Effect. This, of course, assumes that Penny Dreadful has Prime 3 or higher; considering that Penny\u2019s been around for a while, though, that\u2019s a pretty safe assumption. If Penny doesn\u2019t have Prime 3, though, then Penny is stuck using her Avatar rating\u2019s worth of Quintessence, period</div> </div> </div> </div>Quintessence, if employed like any other modifer, cannot be used to bring the effect's difficulty below -3, too. If you don't use any other modifier (out of many, there's a list, such as employing foci, resonance, drawing from the Mythic Threads etc...), you still can use three points of Quintessence (or more, if you have the difficulty raised due to an adversity AND your Avatar rating allows for it), to have it reduced to -3 below the base difficulty for the said spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","user":"Rotwood","date":". 09-20-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:12:36-07:00","id":973933,"title":"","content":"In my games I generally disregard the new innate countermagic rule. To me it simply doesn't make sense, at all.<br /> However, if they have pumped 40 successes on the Ban and that's the end of their defenses, they deserve to get munched. Use any of the many reasonable advise here and see what can BS through your GM. If all fails, bribe a powerful spirit with appropriate theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:54:43-07:00","id":974144,"title":"","content":"Or just toss molotov cocktails in the house until they come out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:27:00-07:00","id":974276,"title":"","content":"Feint a withdrawal and ambush them.<br /> Fight on another day.<br /> Use a trick (damsell in distress, friend hunted by wolves, etc.) to get an ally on the whitelist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T05:58:49-07:00","id":977712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=974276#post974276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feint a withdrawal and ambush them.<br /> Fight on another day.<br /> Use a trick (damsell in distress, friend hunted by wolves, etc.) to get an ally on the whitelist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The players in my chronicle remain hidden 24/7 in their warded farm and they use correspondance to scry/strike their targets from afar, their wards are pretty much impenetrable by anyone who's not a mage(according to them) and there's no way we're going to score 40+ successes, even if our entire sept of wolves were to perform a countermagick roll all together, we're not getting 40+ successes granted majority of us are on 5-7 Rage/Gnosis and that is our dice to countermagick, the players in our chronicle have the concept of roleplay blurred out and tend to make posts here and try to basically grant themselves ''Godmode'' instead of seeking to enhance their general knowledge, it is the sad truth, eitherways; thank you all for your answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:40:47-07:00","id":977752,"title":"","content":"Maybe convince the ST that the rite of abcission will work? It's so well-warded, it can be cauterized from the rest of the territory like a Wyld Threshold and pushed out of reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:08:03-07:00","id":977799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>onedayumay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=977712#post977712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The players in my chronicle remain hidden 24/7 in their warded farm and they use correspondance to scry/strike their targets from afar, their wards are pretty much impenetrable by anyone who's not a mage(according to them) and there's no way we're going to score 40+ successes, even if our entire sept of wolves were to perform a countermagick roll all together, we're not getting 40+ successes granted majority of us are on 5-7 Rage/Gnosis and that is our dice to countermagick, the players in our chronicle have the concept of roleplay blurred out and tend to make posts here and try to basically grant themselves ''Godmode'' instead of seeking to enhance their general knowledge, it is the sad truth, eitherways; thank you all for your answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy solution: stop playing, they sound like chodes.<br /> <br /> Edit: I do like Saur's suggestion, and if I were hell-bent on playing I would try to get this to work. On the other hand, if these players' idea of a good time is to squat in a magical farmhouse and assassinate people with impunity, your game is probably going to be pretty dumb no matter what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 09-28-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:24:06-07:00","id":977856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>onedayumay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972504-penetrating-a-correspondance-ward?p=977712#post977712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The players in my chronicle remain hidden 24/7 in their warded farm and they use correspondance to scry/strike their targets from afar, their wards are pretty much impenetrable by anyone who's not a mage(according to them) and there's no way we're going to score 40+ successes, even if our entire sept of wolves were to perform a countermagick roll all together, we're not getting 40+ successes granted majority of us are on 5-7 Rage/Gnosis and that is our dice to countermagick, the players in our chronicle have the concept of roleplay blurred out and tend to make posts here and try to basically grant themselves ''Godmode'' instead of seeking to enhance their general knowledge, it is the sad truth, eitherways; thank you all for your answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of setup is specifically why Countermagic isn't supposed to operate as all or nothing.<br /> <br /> Aside from various other options mentioned, you might be able to get a powerful Earth Elemental to earthquake the area to break the wards. Similarly, an Air Elemental could conceivably do the same via tornado if the house isn't warded upwards. A powerful localized earthquake though should be enough to destroy/disrupt whatever the physical correspondences are for the Ward/Ban. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:29:58-07:00","id":977860,"title":"","content":"Or they could just hijack a tanker truck full of gasoline, set up an ignition device, and drive it into the farmhouse (jumping out a few moments before it would crash into the farmhouse). If the Mages want to be munchkins, let them deal with that threat. Or, in the case of unusual subtlety, have the Garou call the cops claiming to have seen strange men dragging a teenage girl kicking and screaming into their farmhouse. They could even claim that they were shot at when they tried to save the girl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 09-28-2016, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:35:35-07:00","id":978146,"title":"","content":"Perhaps we are over looking an obvious solution. The gift Open Seal unlocks anything as the wards have a &quot;whitelist&quot; two uses of the gift could open the door and open the ward. This is a bit of a stretch but it solves the problem without resorting to counter magic etc. Other Gifts and Rites to consider: Trackless Wasteland on the farm lands proper any Mage leaving gets lost and can not find their way back(yes they get a roll, but sieges can be fun) Any gift that allows access to the &quot;Dark Umbra&quot; unless the wards were built with both Spirit and Entropy this allows access from the Underworld. The Homid Gift that &quot;recycles&quot; objects into component parts I imagine having a wall turn into piles of wood, brick, and nails would effectively destroy the wards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T20:35:14-07:00","id":978165,"title":"","content":"Or use Create Element to create fire in the farmhouse. I think that the Garou will not be interested on talking to anyone after something like this though. As an ST, I would rule that the Garou should kill the munchkin Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}